{"name":"Derby","hex":"#f9e4c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Derby","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city and unitary authority in Derbyshire, East Midlands, England; formerly the county town .","A suburb of Barnstaple, North Devon district, Devon, England ."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of cheese made in Derby, England."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Derby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Derby","blocks":[{"text":"Derby is a cathedral city and unitary authority area on the River Derwent in Derbyshire, England. Derbyshire is named after Derby, which was its original county town. As a unitary authority, Derby is administratively independent from Derbyshire County Council. The population of Derby is 275,344 (2025)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Derby_Cathedral_at_night.jpg/330px-Derby_Cathedral_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derby"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Derby-_along_Sadler_Gate_%28geograph_7270888%29.jpg/500px-Derby-_along_Sadler_Gate_%28geograph_7270888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Derby-_along_Sadler_Gate_%28geograph_7270888%29.jpg/500px-Derby-_along_Sadler_Gate_%28geograph_7270888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADerby-_along_Sadler_Gate_(geograph_7270888).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Derby%27s_Museum_of_Making.jpg/500px-Derby%27s_Museum_of_Making.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Derby%27s_Museum_of_Making.jpg/1280px-Derby%27s_Museum_of_Making.jpg?utm_source=